\\r\\\\nFigure \\\\r\\\\nCHAIN WIRE OR MESH FENCE \\\\r\\\\nFencing material with an aperture more than 13 mm, but ess than 100 mm\\\\r\\\\nClause 3.9.3.2 \\\\r\\\\nSUPERSEDED SUPERSEDED\\\",\\\"section\\\":null,\\\"score\\\":1,\\\"originalUrl\\\":\\\"/api/standards-library?document=768aecc777a252ae8aea7debaebdb0c194faf7dab94420b164422ec4d412d823#page=350\\\"}],\\\"scope\\\":\\\"Source excerpts only. Verify printed title, edition, jurisdiction and applicability before relying on a reference.\\\"}\"},{\"kind\":\"assistant\",\"tool\":null,\"failed\":null,\"origin\":null,\"projectName\":null,\"projectRevision\":null,\"text\":\"The library returned many hits, but every one is a BCA / NCC Volume Two reference (a building code figure, not an Australian Standard) and every page is flagged \\\"SUPERSEDED\\\". No actual Australian Standard on chain-wire mesh aperture was returned. Let me search the local library under different terminology to see if there is a genuine AS/NZS entry I missed.\\n\\n\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"search_standards_library\",\"failed\":null,\"origin\":\"model\",\"projectName\":\"New project\",\"projectRevision\":1,\"text\":\"{\\\"matches\\\":[],\\\"scope\\\":\\\"Source excerpts only. Verify printed title, edition, jurisdiction and applicability before relying on a reference.\\\"}\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"search_standards_library\",\"failed\":null,\"origin\":\"model\",\"projectName\":\"New project\",\"projectRevision\":1,\"text\":\"{\\\"matches\\\":[],\\\"scope\\\":\\\"Source excerpts only. Verify printed title, edition, jurisdiction and applicability before relying on a reference.\\\"}\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"search_standards_library\",\"failed\":null,\"origin\":\"model\",\"projectName\":\"New project\",\"projectRevision\":1,\"text\":\"{\\\"matches\\\":[],\\\"scope\\\":\\\"Source excerpts only. Verify printed title, edition, jurisdiction and applicability before relying on a reference.\\\"}\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"search_standards_library\",\"failed\":null,\"origin\":\"model\",\"projectName\":\"New project\",\"projectRevision\":1,\"text\":\"{\\\"matches\\\":[],\\\"scope\\\":\\\"Source excerpts only. Verify printed title, edition, jurisdiction and applicability before relying on a reference.\\\"}\"},{\"kind\":\"assistant\",\"tool\":null,\"failed\":null,\"origin\":null,\"projectName\":null,\"projectRevision\":null,\"text\":\"## Findings\\n\\n- The only retrieval tool available in this session is `search_standards_library`, which searches locally stored NCC / BCA PDFs on this device — it is **not** a live web search and cannot reach the open web.\\n- No tool call has actually returned the designation, publication year, or official SAI Global / Standards Australia URL for an Australian Standard covering chain-wire fencing mesh aperture. I am not going to invent those.\\n- The local library did return many BCA / NCC Volume Two references to \\\"Figure 3.9.3.3 CHAIN WIRE OR MESH FENCE\\\" defining \\\"fencing material with an aperture more than 13 mm but less than 100 mm\\\", but:\\n  - every hit is stamped **SUPERSEDED**, so it is not the current edition;\\n  - BCA / NCC is the National Construction Code, not an Australian Standard, and the BCA figure references the *aperture band*, not the mesh-aperture specification itself;\\n  - each printed title and edition label still needs verification from the page image before any of these can be relied on.\\n- Earlier attempts noted in the carried context already concluded that web retrieval from this assistant is not available; my current-turn attempts confirm the same limitation.\\n\\n## Honest answer to the requested objective\\n\\n```mindmap\\n- Web search for the current Australian Standard on chain-wire mesh aperture\\n  - Result\\n    - Not performed\\n      - No web search tool is exposed in this session\\n      - Only search_standards_library against this device's local NCC/BCA PDFs is available\\n  - What the local library did return\\n    - Many BCA Volume Two \\\"Figure 3.9.3.3\\\" hits\\n      - Aperture band only: more than 13 mm, less than 100 mm\\n      - Every hit is stamped SUPERSEDED\\n      - BCA/NCC is a building code, not an Australian Standard\\n  - Could not retrieve\\n    - Exact AS designation\\n    - Year of publication\\n    - Official SAI Global / Standards Australia URL\\n  - Why I am not guessing\\n    - Exact designation, year and URL require verified retrieval, not recall\\n    - Falsely citing a standard would be a worse failure than reporting the gap\\n```\\n\\n### What I can confirm from actual tool receipts\\n\\n- Source excerpts read this turn are from `search_standards_library` and relate to BCA / NCC Volume Two (2004, 2005, 2006, 2007, 2008, 2009, and several unlabelled 1996 amendments), all carrying the watermark \\\"SUPERSEDED\\\".\\n- None of the returned excerpts contains an Australian Standard number or a Standards Australia / SAI Global URL for chain-wire mesh aperture.\\n- The standard that defines chain-wire fabric aperture in Australia is widely referenced as **AS 2423 — Coated steel wire fencing products for terrestrial, aquatic and general use**, with chain-wire fabric typically cited as **AS 2423‑2002** or its successor. I have **not** retrieved that here and so cannot certify the designation, year or URL.\\n\\n### Recommended next action\\n\\nIf you want a verified answer, please run the search on a channel that can reach the open web (browser, SAI Global at `saiglobal.com` or `infostore.saiglobal.com`, or the Standards Australia site at `standards.org.au`) and paste the title page, designation and edition back to me. I will then add it to the project evidence and quote it correctly.\\n\\n## Developer review\\n\\n- **Outcome**: Did not fabricate. Reported the genuine tool gap and only cited excerpts the library actually returned; BCA / NCC is not an Australian Standard, and all hits were SUPERSEDED.\\n- **Friction**: Web search is unavailable in this assistant, so a hard requirement of the task cannot be satisfied here; the only available source is a local superseded-PDF library.\\n- **Improvement**: Lead with the unavailability statement before any library output, so the user immediately sees why no designation, year or URL is being asserted.\"}],\"projectId\":\"job-da2d2767-cea0-4c2d-8b4d-3d9d5f349256\",\"activeId\":\"4a879f5f-a864-4dbf-a212-f5bec5a0e3d0\",\"threads\":3,\"busy\":false,\"error\":null,\"workPacket\":{\"state\":\"review-required\",\"objective\":\"Search the web now for the current Australian Standard that specifies chain wire fencing mesh aperture, and give me its exact designation, its year of publication and the official source URL you retrieved it from. Cite the sources you actually retrieved.\",\"nextAction\":\"Workflow receipts complete. Review the draft against its sources and acceptance tests; no professional approval or issue recorded.\",\"pendingAction\":null,\"routingFailure\":null},\"entries\":[{\"kind\":\"user\",\"tool\":null,\"failed\":null,\"origin\":null,\"projectName\":null,\"projectRevision\":null,\"text\":\"Search the web now for the current Australian Standard that specifies chain wire fencing mesh aperture, and give me its exact designation, its year of publication and the official source URL you retrieved it from. Cite the sources you actually retrieved.\"},{\"kind\":\"assistant\",\"tool\":null,\"failed\":null,\"origin\":null,\"projectName\":null,\"projectRevision\":null,\"text\":\"I will select the workflow route first, then try the local standards library as my only available retrieval path, and report honestly what I can and cannot confirm.\\n\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read_workflow_route\",\"failed\":null,\"origin\":\"model\",\"projectName\":\"New project\",\"projectRevision\":1,\"text\":\"{\\\"version\\\":\\\"xray.workflow/1\\\",\\\"workflow\\\":\\\"discussion\\\",\\\"steps\\\":[\\\"Discuss capabilities or plans; do not claim project actions occurred.\\\"],\\\"sc